# The safety tests: each line is `path|function`, a test that guards the volume rule (the
# three-quarters glide, the climb's cancellation), the firmware-update refusals, the passphrase
# refusals (function 250 never sent raw, never a control, never exposed) with the layers below the
# profile loader that refuse it on their own, the capture's argv, the capture file's scrub (the
# passphrase and the unit ids it must never hold), the remote views (the passphrase never reaches
# a remote view) or the device presets' questions (a built-in setting's rise and a slot's recall
# over MCP, and a save).
# `make safety-tests` fails if a listed file no longer defines the function, so none of these
# tests can be removed or renamed without someone noticing. To rename one, change its line in the
# same commit; to remove one, say why in the commit message.
bins/svolder/tests/device_cli.rs|raw_set_of_firmware_update_is_refused
